{"event_id":"EVT-000032","timestamp_utc":"2026-09-15T11:54:12.952Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260915T092108806520Z","run_id":"RUN-IMO-124-20260915T115326002825Z","requirement_id":"IMO-124","event_type":"iteration_completed","iteration":1,"architecture":"FULL_REPAIR_V2","generation_run":"RUN_01","mode":"INITIAL_GENERATION","static_valid":true,"validator_accept":false,"matcher_activated":false,"decision":"REVISE","feedback":"[LOGIC] MainShape / sh:or: The conditional obligations are encoded as an OR between a SPARQL branch that passes when the applicability condition is true and a branch containing the obligations. Consequently, an applicable ship satisfies the first branch and can bypass the 12-nautical-mile threshold, distance recording, and food-waste prohibition. Required change: Encode the implication so that when operatingArea is Antarctic_area and marpolAnnexVRegulation6Point1DischargeOccurs is true, all required constraints are enforced; otherwise the conditional constraint passes. | [INVENTED_CONSTRAINT] MainShape / nltl:antarcticArea: The candidate makes antarcticArea a mandatory, single-valued xsd:string input even though the normalized requirement's applicability condition uses operating_area = Antarctic_area and does not require a separate antarcticArea field. This can reject conforming ship data lacking that extraneous property. Required change: Remove the unconditional minCount/maxCount constraint on antarcticArea unless it is explicitly part of the applicability condition, and use the required operatingArea value directly. | [INVENTED_CONSTRAINT] MainShape / nltl:nearbyIceConcentration: The candidate requires a nearbyIceConcentration quantity and constrains it to be greater than 0.1. The requirement only defines areas with ice concentration exceeding one-tenth as the reference for the required distance record; it does not require a separate nearbyIceConcentration value or impose that threshold on a ship property. Required change: Remove the mandatory nearbyIceConcentration property constraint; retain only the required recorded distance from areas whose ice concentration exceeds one-tenth. | [INVENTED_CONSTRAINT] MainShape / nltl:iceConcentration: The candidate requires a separate iceConcentration quantity greater than 0.1. The requirement requires recording the distance from areas exceeding one-tenth concentration, but does not require this standalone concentration value on the ship. Required change: Remove the mandatory iceConcentration property constraint unless the model explicitly represents and requires the concentration value as part of the distance evidence.","stalled":false,"oscillation_detected":false,"current_issues":[{"category":"LOGIC","location":"MainShape / sh:or","problem":"The conditional obligations are encoded as an OR between a SPARQL branch that passes when the applicability condition is true and a branch containing the obligations. Consequently, an applicable ship satisfies the first branch and can bypass the 12-nautical-mile threshold, distance recording, and food-waste prohibition.","required_change":"Encode the implication so that when operatingArea is Antarctic_area and marpolAnnexVRegulation6Point1DischargeOccurs is true, all required constraints are enforced; otherwise the conditional constraint passes.","regression_guard":"Preserve enforcement of every obligation for the applicable Antarctic discharge case.","blocking":true,"needs_vocabulary_resolution":false,"source":"SEMANTIC"},{"category":"INVENTED_CONSTRAINT","location":"MainShape / nltl:antarcticArea","problem":"The candidate makes antarcticArea a mandatory, single-valued xsd:string input even though the normalized requirement's applicability condition uses operating_area = Antarctic_area and does not require a separate antarcticArea field. This can reject conforming ship data lacking that extraneous property.","required_change":"Remove the unconditional minCount/maxCount constraint on antarcticArea unless it is explicitly part of the applicability condition, and use the required operatingArea value directly.","regression_guard":"Do not add mandatory applicability inputs beyond operatingArea and the MARPOL discharge status.","blocking":true,"needs_vocabulary_resolution":false,"source":"SEMANTIC"},{"category":"INVENTED_CONSTRAINT","location":"MainShape / nltl:nearbyIceConcentration","problem":"The candidate requires a nearbyIceConcentration quantity and constrains it to be greater than 0.1. The requirement only defines areas with ice concentration exceeding one-tenth as the reference for the required distance record; it does not require a separate nearbyIceConcentration value or impose that threshold on a ship property.","required_change":"Remove the mandatory nearbyIceConcentration property constraint; retain only the required recorded distance from areas whose ice concentration exceeds one-tenth.","regression_guard":"Preserve the one-tenth condition as the definition of the referenced ice areas, not as an additional mandatory ship measurement.","blocking":true,"needs_vocabulary_resolution":false,"source":"SEMANTIC"},{"category":"INVENTED_CONSTRAINT","location":"MainShape / nltl:iceConcentration","problem":"The candidate requires a separate iceConcentration quantity greater than 0.1. The requirement requires recording the distance from areas exceeding one-tenth concentration, but does not require this standalone concentration value on the ship.","required_change":"Remove the mandatory iceConcentration property constraint unless the model explicitly represents and requires the concentration value as part of the distance evidence.","regression_guard":"Keep the required distance evidence distinct from an unrequired standalone concentration measurement.","blocking":true,"needs_vocabulary_resolution":false,"source":"SEMANTIC"}],"generator_elapsed_ms":34532.635,"validator_elapsed_ms":12200.048}
